<%# One banked lesson in the Insight Bank. Local: grade (a banked ActionGrade). The
    left border + disposition badge read the binary good/not signal; the meta line
    traces it back to whatever it was mined from and whether it is Alex's grade or
    the McRitchie audit of Alex.

    A grade targets EITHER a raw action OR a narrated activity (ActionGrade's XOR), so
    read the provenance from whichever is set — an activity grade has no agent_action
    (dereferencing it unconditionally 500'd the whole bank). Both nil means the
    target was deleted (has_many :nullify), so the lesson outlives its source. %>
<% source = grade.insight_source %>
<div class="hb-insight <%= "is-not" if grade.not_good? %>" data-test="insight">
  <div class="hb-isl">
    <span><%= grade.slug %></span>
    <span class="hb-disp <%= grade.good? ? "good" : "not" %>"><%= grade.disposition.upcase %></span>
    <span class="hb-grader"><%= grade.alex? ? "Alex" : "McR → Alex" %></span>
  </div>
  <%# The separator is LITERAL template markup, so the browser gets the entity while
      each interpolated value rides ERB's automatic output escaping. Both values are
      untrusted — `insight_label` falls back to an action's unvalidated `event_slug`/
      `kind`, and `task_slug` derives from operator- and agent-written titles (neither
      column has a format validation). The earlier spelling built ONE string and marked
      it whole with `.html_safe`, which switched escaping off exactly where the
      untrusted value landed and let markup render as live DOM (Brakeman: High XSS x2).
      Do not "simplify" this back into an interpolated `.html_safe` string. Equally,
      do not fold the separator into the Ruby expression — a bare "&middot;" inside an
      output tag is escaped and renders as the literal text on the page. %>
  <div class="hb-imeta">
    <% if source %>
      from <%= grade.activity_grade? ? "activity " : "" %>#<%= source.seq %>
      <% if grade.insight_label.present? %> &middot; <%= grade.insight_label %><% end %>
      <% if source.task_slug.present? %> &middot; <%= source.task_slug %><% end %>
    <% else %>
      source since removed
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% if grade.long_form.present? %>
    <div class="hb-ilg"><%= grade.long_form %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
